3 Method We first review Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT) and Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR), to contextualize our approach. Then we detail the training objective, optimization process, reward shaping, and mechanisms for enforcing structured reasoning trace of our proposed method. 3.1 Preliminaries: Standard Paradigms for Reasoning Training Supervised Fine-Tuning (SFT). SFT adapts a pre-trained model π θ \pi_{	heta} to mimic expert demonstrations from a dataset 𝒟 \mathcal{D} , where each instance is a triplet ( x , z ⋆ , y ⋆ ) (x,z^{\star},y^{\star}) of an input question, an expert reasoning trace, and a final answer. The objective is to maximize the conditional log-likelihood of the expert sequence o ⋆ = ( z ⋆ , y ⋆ ) o^{\star}=(z^{\star},y^{\star}) , expressed as: J SFT ​ ( θ ) = 𝔼 ( x , z ⋆ , y ⋆ ) ∼ 𝒟 ​ [ log ⁡ π θ ​ ( z ⋆ , y ⋆ | x ) ] . J_{	ext{SFT}}(	heta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,z^{\star},y^{\star})\sim\mathcal{D}}\left[\log\pi_{	heta}(z^{\star},y^{\star}|x)ight]. (1) As language models are auto-regressive, this log-likelihood over the token sequence o ⋆ = ( t 1 , … , t N ) o^{\star}=(t_{1},\dots,t_{N}) is decomposed as: log ⁡ π θ ​ ( o ⋆ | x ) = ∑ i = 1 N log ⁡ π θ ​ ( t i | x , t < i ) . \log\pi_{	heta}(o^{\star}|x)=\sum_{i=1}^{N}\log\pi_{	heta}(t_{i}|x,t_{<i}). (2) This phase instills a strong prior for reasoning structure, preparing it for subsequent optimization. Reinforcement Learning with Verifiable Rewards (RLVR). Unlike imitation-based SFT, Reinforcement Learning (RL) optimizes the policy π θ \pi_{	heta} to maximize an expected reward R ⁡ ( x , o ) R(x,o) for a generated output o = ( z , y ) o=(z,y) . The general objective is: max θ 𝔼 o ∼ π θ ( ⋅ | x ) [ R ( x , o ) ] . \max_{	heta}\mathbb{E}_{o\sim\pi_{	heta}(\cdot|x)}[R(x,o)]. (3) In RLVR, the reward is determined by an external verifier assessing the correctness of the final answer y y against the ground truth y ⋆ y^{\star} . The reward is typically binary: R Verifier ( y ; y ⋆ ) = 𝟏 {